{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB01030 - MONDO_20538",
  "verbalization": "Topotecan, a topoisomerase I inhibitor, is implicated in the treatment of ovarian cancers, including malignant dysgerminomatous germ cell tumors of the ovary. The evidence suggests that Topotecan may be repurposed for this condition, as it is indicated for ovarian adenocarcinoma and granulosa cell tumors, both of which are related to dysgerminomatous germ cell tumors. The shared indication for Altretamine, a drug that shares a common pathway with Topotecan, further supports a potential mechanistic link. The presence of a common pathway involving topoisomerase inhibition and the related indication for Altretamine indicates that Topotecan may exert its effects through a mechanism that is relevant to the pathogenesis of malignant dysgerminomatous germ cell tumors of the ovary. The integration of these pathways suggests that Topotecan could be a viable candidate for repurposing in this context, provided the underlying biological mechanisms are well understood and validated.",
